    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1092">

                <pb facs="0907" n="897" xml:id="pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Gleysteen, Culver: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Dairen</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Paddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dairen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-01T15:00:00+09:00">August 1, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 2—9:59 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>227. Last information regarding communication to Soviet Foreign Office re
                    Gleysteen detention was Moscow’s 1490 to Department, repeated Nanking 65.<anchor
                        n="47" xml:id="d1092-f1"/> Consulate wonders if any new development
                    regarding this matter.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 227, repeated Moscow 121, Nanking 164.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paddock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
